For the ByteVec case, the immutable borrow `v.get_ref().as_slice()` is tied to `&self.inner` borrow which must live as long as '1 (returned). And the mutable borrow of self.inner also lives for '1. Conflict.

Solution: compute replay differently per case. For ByteVec, instead of borrowing from self.inner, note that as_body converts ByteVec → ByteSlice(v.get_ref()) — the inner of the result borrows self.inner mutably-reborrowed... hmm wait, actually `BodyInner::ByteVec(v) => BodyInner::ByteSlice(v.get_ref())` — here `v: &mut Cursor<Vec<u8>>`, `v.get_ref(): &Vec<u8>` borrowed from `v` which is a reborrow of self.inner for '1. So the result's inner ALREADY borrows self.inner for '1 immutably-ish (through the &mut reborrow chain).

Key insight: for the ByteVec case, the replay slice is the SAME data as the resulting inner ByteSlice. So I can set replay after constructing inner... but I can't easily re-borrow.

Alternative: compute replay from the RESULT inner:

```rust
